<title>BANGLADESH: Port workers in Bangladesh call off strike.</title>
<headline>Port workers in Bangladesh call off strike.</headline>
<dateline>KHULNA, Bangladesh 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Workers at Bangladesh's southern Mongla port on Wednesday called off a strike after reaching an agreement with port authorities, officials said.</p>
<p>Nearly 6,500 workers walked out over a wage dispute on November 11, leaving at least 12 ships, carrying fertiliser, cement and general cargo, stranded at the port.</p>
<p>The officials said the workers agreed to resume handling cargo from Wednesday evening after a deal reached with the Dock Workers Association on their demands, including higher wages and benefits and the employment of more dock labourers.</p>
</text>
